--! A test platform's one capability: make every later `child_process.spawn`
--! give a child that starts and whose input pipe fails with an error code
--! of the caller's choosing, by the route Node takes for a write that
--! failed. It reaches what `ChildProcess.run` does with an error of the
--! input pipe, with no real pipe and no race.

--| From now on, every `child_process.spawn` gives a child that starts, and
--| whose standard input fails its first write with an error whose `code`
--| is the given one. After that the child writes `after the write` and
--| exits 0.
pub foreign impure failInput : String → ⊤
